{"description":"Retain messages addressed to a device that is not connected, and deliver them when it returns.\n\nCoordinator side: a per-recipient inbox with monotonic positions, acknowledgement, a retention TTL and a size cap that refuses rather than silently failing. Client side: an outbox so a message composed while disconnected is transmitted on reconnect.\n\nDelivery is at-least-once on the wire and deduplicated at the receiver by ULID. Exactly-once is not attempted at the transport layer; it is achieved by making redelivery harmless.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. A message sent to an offline device is delivered when it reconnects.\n2. A device reconnecting twice receives each pending message once.\n3. A message composed while the sender is offline is delivered after the sender reconnects.\n4. Resumption transfers only messages after the acknowledged position, verified by counting what crosses the wire — not merely by what the user sees.\n5. Messages past the retention TTL are removed and the removal is logged.\n6. Reaching the size cap produces an explicit refusal to both sender and logs; the coordinator does not grow past it and does not fail silently."}